## Who we are

West of Mauritius (westofmauritius.mu) is published in Mauritius by Olivier who is its founder and editor. He is responsible for the personal data described on this page. Contact: [hello@westofmauritius.mu](mailto:hello@westofmauritius.mu).

## What we collect and why

**Property enquiries.** When you send the enquiry form in Living in the West we store the details you give us: your name and email address and phone or WhatsApp number (if given) as well as your country and budget and timeframe and areas of interest. We also store your message and newsletter choice and language and the page you came from. With your consent we share these details with selected property developers and estate agents on the west coast of Mauritius so that they can contact you about your enquiry. Legal basis: your consent. You can withdraw it at any time by writing to us. This does not affect sharing that already took place.

**Contact form.** We store your name and email address and subject and message in order to reply. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in answering messages.

**Newsletter.** We store your email address and language and the page where you signed up. We send a confirmation link first and nothing is sent until you confirm. Every newsletter contains an unsubscribe link. Legal basis: your consent.

**WhatsApp group.** If you ask to join our west coast WhatsApp group we store your name and WhatsApp number and whether you live here or are moving or visit often. We also store your language and the page where you signed up so that we can invite you. In a WhatsApp group other members can see your number. Legal basis: your consent.

**Protection against spam.** To limit automated submissions we keep a scrambled (salted hash) form of your IP address for up to 24 hours. It is not used for anything else.

**Visitor statistics.** We use Umami which counts visits without cookies and without collecting personal data.

**Maps.** Maps are loaded from OpenFreeMap; your browser connects to their servers to fetch map images.

## Who receives your data

- Property developers and estate agents on the west coast only for property enquiries and only with your consent.
- Service providers who process data on our behalf: Cloudflare (hosting) and Neon (database) and Resend (email) and Umami (statistics). Some of them process data outside Mauritius and the European Union. We rely on the data processing terms each of them offers including standard contractual clauses where they apply.
- WhatsApp (Meta) for members of the WhatsApp group under WhatsApp's own terms.

We never sell personal data. We never share contact messages or newsletter addresses or WhatsApp numbers with developers or agents.

## How long we keep it

- Property enquiries: 24 months after your last contact with us.
- Contact messages: 12 months.
- Newsletter addresses: until you unsubscribe.
- WhatsApp group requests: until you leave the group or ask us to delete them.
- Scrambled IP addresses for spam protection: 24 hours.

## Your rights

You can ask for access to your data or its correction or deletion or restriction or portability. You can object to its use and withdraw your consent at any time. Write to [hello@westofmauritius.mu](mailto:hello@westofmauritius.mu). You may also complain to the Data Protection Office of Mauritius or to the data protection authority where you live (for example the CNIL in France or the ICO in the United Kingdom or the Information Regulator in South Africa).

